HST Office: the digital signatures dialog says when a signature is not verified, and the certificate viewer no longer calls it valid.

The signatures list showed the signer's name for every signature, with only a small icon telling a valid
signature from one that does not verify (content changed after signing, an incomplete copy, a certificate that is
not trusted or was not checked). The certificate viewer opened from that row checked the certificate on its own
(fetching issuer and revocation data online) and could say "This certificate is validated." for a signature that
is not valid. Now the row says "(not verified)" after the name unless the signature and its certificate are valid,
and the viewer opened from such a row says that the signature is not valid and its details are about the
certificate only, without the certificate check and without the certification path page. The logic and strings are
in xmlsecurity/source/hst/signaturestatus.*; the upstream files only call it.

License: the new files xmlsecurity/source/hst/signaturestatus.* are LicenseRef-HST-Proprietary; the upstream files
remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-signature-not-verified.py with xmlsecurity/qa/unit/signing/data/bad.odt.
